cije-vpsinstallerweb
====================

Browser UI for the **Cije VPS Installer**. This repository is a separate
application from the CLI (`cije-vps-installer` / `debian_vps_setup`). It does
not replace that project.

The web layer saves a JSON config, then calls the vendored CLI package for
setup, resume, status, DNS help, per-component troubleshoot, and config
snapshots. Install logic lives in `vendor/debian_vps_setup` (`import
debian_vps_setup`).

**This UI must run on the target Debian VPS when you want a real install.** It
is not a remote provisioner. By default it only dry-runs against a fake
`--root` so a laptop or CI job cannot `apt`/`systemctl` a live machine.

Safety
------

- Default mode is **dry-run** with `CIJE_WEB_ROOT` under the data directory.
- Live mode requires **all** of: `CIJE_WEB_ALLOW_LIVE=1`, `CIJE_WEB_DRY_RUN=0`,
  and `CIJE_WEB_ROOT=/`.
- Do not run live mode on a workstation, a shared host, or an already-configured
  production server. Use a fresh Debian 12/13 VPS, as the CLI README states.
- Bind the HTTP server to **localhost** and put TLS on a reverse proxy. The
  shared token is not a substitute for HTTPS on a public address.
- Config JSON and install reports contain passwords. Files are written mode 600
  when the OS allows it.

Requirements
------------

- Python 3.11+
- The vendored `debian_vps_setup` tree (shipped in this repo)
- For a **real** install: root on the VPS, same hardware/OS needs as the CLI

Quick start (local / safe)
--------------------------

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e '.[dev]'
export CIJE_WEB_TOKEN=dev-token
python -m cije_vpsinstallerweb --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18765
```

Open `http://127.0.0.1:18765/login` and sign in with `dev-token`.

You should see a dashboard and a setup wizard (domain, panel, webmail including
Roundcube / Usermin / SnappyMail / Cypht, Mailbaby, SSL, VNC). Starting an
install in this mode streams dry-run logs; it will not install packages.

Environment
-----------

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|----------|---------|---------|
| `CIJE_WEB_TOKEN` | generated at startup | Shared secret (cookie, `Authorization: Bearer`, or `X-API-Token`) |
| `CIJE_WEB_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Bind address |
| `CIJE_WEB_PORT` | `18765` | Bind port |
| `CIJE_WEB_DATA` | `./data` | Web config + logs |
| `CIJE_WEB_ROOT` | `$CIJE_WEB_DATA/fake-root` | Filesystem root passed to `Runner` |
| `CIJE_WEB_DRY_RUN` | `1` | Pass `dry_run=True` into the CLI runner |
| `CIJE_WEB_ALLOW_LIVE` | `0` | Must be `1` before a live root is accepted |

If `CIJE_WEB_TOKEN` is unset, the process prints a one-time token. Set the
variable for anything that should survive a restart.

Reverse proxy (TLS)
-------------------

Keep uvicorn on loopback. Example nginx snippet:

```nginx
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name installer.example.com;
    # ssl_certificate ...;
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:18765;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header Authorization $http_authorization;
        proxy_buffering off;
        proxy_read_timeout 3600;
    }
}
```

Terminate TLS here. Do not forward the app port to the public internet.

systemd
-------

An **example** unit lives at `contrib/systemd/cije-vpsinstallerweb.service`.
It is documentation only: copy it, set `CIJE_WEB_TOKEN`, and leave it
**disabled** until you intend to run the UI on that VPS.

```bash
sudo cp contrib/systemd/cije-vpsinstallerweb.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
# sudo systemctl enable --now cije-vpsinstallerweb   # only after editing the unit
```

Pages and API
-------------

| UI | JSON |
|----|------|
| `/` dashboard | `GET /api/health` (no auth), `GET /api/meta` |
| `/wizard` | `GET/PUT /api/config` |
| `/logs` | `POST /api/install`, `GET /api/jobs/{id}/stream` (SSE) |
| `/status` | `GET /api/status`, `GET /api/report`, `POST /api/test` |
| `/dns` | `GET /api/dns` |
| `/troubleshoot` | `POST /api/troubleshoot` |
| `/backup` | `GET/POST /api/backup`, `POST /api/backup/{id}/restore` |

Auth: `X-API-Token`, `Authorization: Bearer …`, `?token=` (SSE), or the login
cookie.

What the web layer does **not** do
----------------------------------

- Rewrite Virtualmin / 1Panel / Postfix / webmail installers
- Image the disk or restore mailboxes / uploaded site files
- Talk to a remote VPS over SSH; run it **on** the machine you are building

Tests
-----

```bash
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

These hit the FastAPI app with a fake `--root` and dry-run jobs. They do not
need root and they must not run `apt` on the host.

Vendor
------

`vendor/debian_vps_setup` is a copy of the CLI package (v1.1.0). Refresh it
from the CLI repository when that package changes. Keep this repo named
**cije-vpsinstallerweb**.

